---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="mdbase Connect"
  description="mdbase Connect is the account that syncs and shares your Markdown collections. Choose Cloud copy or Private for each collection, approve apps, share with people, and add devices."
  current="connect"
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <h1>mdbase Connect</h1>
    <p class="page-intro__lede">
      Connect is the account that syncs and shares your collections. This page
      explains what you choose for each collection, what mdbase can read, and
      how apps, people and devices get access.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="sync-options">
    <h2 id="sync-options">Cloud copy or Private</h2>
    <p>
      When you turn on sync for a collection, every device that syncs it keeps a
      complete copy as ordinary files and works offline. Each change is locked
      on the device before it leaves. mdbase passes it to your other devices
      and can’t read it. You choose one of two options for each collection:
    </p>
    <dl class="glossary-list">
      <div>
        <dt>Cloud copy</dt>
        <dd>
          The default for new accounts. mdbase also keeps a readable copy of the
          collection and holds its key. Web apps keep working while your devices
          are off, and a new device joins when you sign in.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Private</dt>
        <dd>
          End-to-end encrypted. Only your devices hold the key, so mdbase can’t
          read the collection. Apps reach it through one of your devices, so one
          of them must be online, such as a computer running the
          <a href="/downloads/">desktop app</a>.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <p>
      You can switch a collection between the two later. One synced collection
      is free. The <a href="/security/">security page</a> lists exactly what
      mdbase stores and can read in each case.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="devices">
    <h2 id="devices">Add a device</h2>
    <p>
      For a Cloud copy collection, sign in on the new device. Once your account
      approves it, the device receives the collection key and downloads its
      copy. None of your other devices need to be online.
    </p>
    <p>
      For Private collections, you set an encryption password when you create
      your first one, and mdbase shows you a recovery key once. Keep the
      recovery key in a password manager or on paper. To add a device, sign in
      and enter your encryption password or the recovery key. mdbase stores your
      key only in a form locked with your password, so it can’t reset the
      password for you. The recovery key is how you get back in if you forget it.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you’d prefer mdbase to store no copy of that key, turn on strict mode.
      You then approve each new device from one you already have, by checking
      that both screens show the same six-digit code.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you lose a device, remove it from your account. The collection gets a
      new key, so the removed device receives no further changes. It keeps the
      files it already had.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="apps">
    <h2 id="apps">Apps ask first</h2>
    <p>
      An app asks for access to one collection and lists the operations it
      needs, such as finding, creating and editing records. You choose the
      collection and see what the app asks for before you approve it.
    </p>
    <p>
      The permission is recorded with the collection, and every copy checks it:
      your devices and, for Cloud copy, mdbase’s copy. In a Private collection,
      a new permission only takes effect once one of your devices has approved
      it.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can narrow or revoke a permission at any time. Removing an app
      never removes the collection, and your other apps keep using it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="share-a-collection">
    <h2 id="share-a-collection">Share a collection</h2>
    <p>
      Owners can invite people as viewers, who can read, or editors, who can
      read and change records. Both Cloud copy and Private collections can be
      shared. Open the collection’s sharing controls in the
      <a href="https://editor.mdbase.dev/">mdbase Editor</a> and invite someone
      by email. They need a registered, verified Connect account.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each member’s devices keep a full copy, and members can connect their own
      apps within the role you gave them. In a Private collection, an owner or
      editor approves a new member’s first device by comparing a six-digit code
      with them, in person or on a call.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can change a member’s role or remove them at any time. A removed
      member stops receiving changes and keeps the files they already had.
    </p>
    <p>
      Sharing covers a whole collection. To share part of one, make a separate
      collection. Edits that people make at the same time are combined field by
      field, and edits that change the same field are held for review. There is
      no live co-editing of a note.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="moving-from-the-connector">
    <h2 id="moving-from-the-connector">If you used Connect before</h2>
    <p>
      Existing accounts move to the new sync system in an announced migration
      window. Your files stay where they are.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Collections hosted by Connect</strong> become Cloud copy
        collections, with their records, files, record IDs and members. Folders
        that mirrored them join the new collection once the desktop app is
        updated. Edits that weren’t uploaded yet arrive then, or are held for
        review if the record also changed elsewhere.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Local collections served by the Connector</strong> stay on your
        computer with sync off. The updated <a href="/downloads/">desktop app</a>{" "}
        takes them over and keeps their files and record IDs. Nothing is
        uploaded. You’ll be asked to turn sync on and choose Cloud copy or
        Private. Until then, apps reach the collection through that computer
        while it’s running.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Apps</strong> need their current versions. Older versions can’t
        reach migrated collections and will ask you to update, and you may need
        to approve some apps again.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="get-started">
    <h2 id="get-started">Get started</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/beta/">Create a Connect account</a>,{" "}
      <a href="/downloads/">download the desktop app</a>, or{" "}
      <a href="https://connect.mdbase.dev/login">sign in</a> to manage an
      existing account. See the <a href="/apps/">apps</a> that work with mdbase
      collections.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
